<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Nadruvians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1277 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people of Nadruvia, between the Pregolya and Neman rivers, among the last to be conquered by the Teutonic Knights.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nadruvia lay in the north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neman">Neman</a>, in what is now the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaliningrad-oblast">Kaliningrad</a> region. Its people were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Prussians</a>, known mainly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-dusburg">Peter of Dusburg's</a> chronicle, which describes a sacred site called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romowe">Romowe</a> somewhere in the territory, though its existence is debated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived from farming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and forest resources, under local nobles with hillforts. Their land bordered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/scalovians">Scalovia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sudovians">Sudovia</a> and was close to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> conquered Nadruvia in 1274-1277. Much of the population fled or was resettled, and the region became a thinly peopled frontier of the Order's state, later repopulated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanians">Lithuanians</a> and Germans.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nadruvians.jpg" alt="Nadruvians" width="320" height="225"><figcaption>Image: Renata3 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prussian_clans_13th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1277 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>, <a href="/countries/lithuania">Lithuania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nadruvia, Nadrovia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1038&amp;focus=nadruvians" aria-label="Nadruvians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5615 202 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nadruvians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5935 458h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5935 458h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1038&amp;focus=nadruvians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

